@startuml
title 2. Place Totem (Socket)

legend top
This diagram shows the totem placement process during the game phase.
The client sends a PlaceTotemRequest specifying the selected offer slot.
The request is handled by the Controller and delegated to the current InGamePhase,
which invokes the Game model. The model validates turn order and slot availability.
If the move is valid, the updated game state is returned; otherwise, an error is generated.
endlegend

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #2F4F4F
    LifeLineBorderColor #708090
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
    ParticipantBorderColor #5F6F7F
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAEFF7
    ActorBorderColor #5F6F7F
    ActorBackgroundColor #EAEFF7
    GroupBorderColor #444444
    GroupBackgroundColor #FDFDFD
    BoxBorderColor #7F8C8D
    BoxBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
}

actor Player

box "Client Node" #DDF3F4
participant View
participant VirtualSocketServer
end box

box "Server Node" #F7F5D6
participant "SocketClientHandler\n(VirtualView)" as Handler
participant Controller
participant InGamePhase
participant "Game\n(Model)" as Game
end box

Player -> View : selectOfferSlot(slotID)
View -> VirtualSocketServer : placeTotem(nickname, slotID)
VirtualSocketServer -> Handler : PlaceTotemRequest(nickname, slotID)

note right of Handler
Network message received\nfrom the client.
end note

Handler -> Controller : placeTotem(nickname, slotID)
Controller -> InGamePhase : handlePlaceTotem(this, nickname, slotID)
InGamePhase -> Game : placeTotem(player, slotID)

alt [Valid placement]
    Game --> InGamePhase : return
    InGamePhase --> Controller : success
    Controller -> Handler : GameUpdated(gameState)
    Handler -> VirtualSocketServer : GameUpdated(gameState)
    VirtualSocketServer -> View : updateBoard(gameState)
else [Invalid placement]
    Game --> InGamePhase : throw InvalidMoveException
    InGamePhase --> Controller : propagate exception
    Controller -> Handler : Error("Slot occupied or wrong turn")
    Handler -> VirtualSocketServer : Error("Slot occupied or wrong turn")
    VirtualSocketServer -> View : showError("Slot occupied or wrong turn")
end

note right of Game
The model validates:
- current phase
- active player
- slot availability
Then it updates the game state.
end note

@enduml